2, the record in Kay County runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids, January to February and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years, and April to May did in 30. In 2025 on the middle, November to December came in at 30% of normal and June to July at 194%. Every grid had its driest year in 1956, with grid 19931 at 46%.</p>"}
